      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/revit/find-elements",
      "title": "Find Elements by Category",
      "description": "Count placed elements by category and group returned family and type only when itemsComplete is true. A truncated result is not a complete inventory. Selector helper: find element ids by scope (viewId OR sheetNumber) and filters. Supports sheet-region targeting, visible-text search, and bounded document discovery across instance name, family, type, category, and Mark. identityTerms uses exact phrase or at-least-half meaningful-token overlap and returns the matched evidence. physicalElementsOnly excludes view-owned/non-model artifacts; topLevelInstancesOnly excludes nested children. expandIdentityAcronymsInParameters performs a second, category-grounded scan for delimiter-bounded phrase acronyms in string parameters and returns the exact parameter evidence; it never expands without a first-pass physical identity seed. includeGeometry adds each physical result's world-space location, axis-aligned bounding box, orientation, type, level, host, and location-curve length/straightness. Agent projections expose routeCurveCandidates for bounded duct/pipe edit discovery; connector topology must still be verified before mutation. Body: {viewId?,sheetNumber?,includeSheetElements?,includeViewportElements?,sheetRegions?:[{minU,minV,maxU,maxV}],regionPaddingFt?,category?,categories?,typeNameContains?,familyNameContains?,nameContains?,markContains?,textContains?,identityTerms?:string[],physicalElementsOnly?,topLevelInstancesOnly?,expandIdentityAcronymsInParameters?,includeGeometry?,limit?}.",
      "group": "Query",
      "example": "find physical air-terminal instances with world geometry anywhere in this project",
      "risk": "low",
      "required_fields": [],
      "optional_fields": [
        "viewId",
        "sheetNumber",
        "includeSheetElements",
        "includeViewportElements",
        "sheetRegions",
        "regionPaddingFt",
        "category",
        "categories",
        "typeNameContains",
        "familyNameContains",
        "nameContains",
        "markContains",
        "textContains",
        "identityTerms",
        "physicalElementsOnly",
        "topLevelInstancesOnly",
        "expandIdentityAcronymsInParameters",
        "includeGeometry",
        "limit"
      ],
      "enums": {},
      "units": [
        {
          "unit": "feet",
          "fields": [
            "items[*].geometry.locationPoint",
            "items[*].geometry.locationCurve.start",
            "items[*].geometry.locationCurve.end",
            "items[*].geometry.locationCurve.midpoint",
            "items[*].geometry.locationCurve.lengthFt",
            "items[*].geometry.boundingBox.min",
            "items[*].geometry.boundingBox.max",
            "items[*].geometry.boundingBox.center",
            "items[*].geometry.boundingBox.size"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Scope precedence: if viewId is provided it is used; otherwise sheetNumber scopes to views placed on that sheet (viewports).",
        "For redline workflows, provide sheetRegions (sheet UV boxes) to return only elements overlapping mapped markup areas.",
        "Categories are BuiltInCategory tokens like OST_Doors, OST_TitleBlocks, OST_GenericModel.",
        "For ordinary whole-document object discovery, identityTerms searches instance name, family, type, category, and Mark while preserving matched-term/field evidence; combine physicalElementsOnly and topLevelInstancesOnly to exclude schedules, legends, annotations, and nested child components.",
        "expandIdentityAcronymsInParameters is seed-gated: only categories with a physical first-pass identity match are scanned for delimiter-bounded phrase acronyms in string parameters, and exact parameter-name/value evidence is returned.",
        "includeGeometry=true returns model/world coordinates, transformed axis-aligned bounding boxes, FamilyInstance facing/hand orientation, and type/level/host ids for bounded project-wide spatial analysis without requiring a visible view export."
      ],
